From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohamed Ahmed <mohamedahmedegypt2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:03:55 +0400
Subject: drm/nouveau/dispnv50: work around Turing memory clock scanout
 glitches

Turing bug 2052012 can corrupt cursor or overlay scanout during a memory
clock switch when no primary window is active. Use the display capability
bit to enable the mid-frame/DWCF watermark workaround on affected GPUs.

Track cursor surface attachment separately from visibility because an
off-screen cursor still needs the workaround. Disable the watermarks with
the plane update, but restore them in a separate update after the plane
wait. Restoring them in the same update could leave the old scanout
unprotected during the transition.

Signed-off-by: Mohamed Ahmed <mohamedahmedegypt2001@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7f71df775e84623fa75a7571bcaf06b93e05857f)
